{"run_id":"run_e5dc9b72def5","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"The compensation review process document doesn't list detailed banding steps. Here's everything it says:\n\n- **How often:** Reviews happen twice a year.\n- **Banding recommendations:** Managers submit them through the People Operations portal.\n- **Who can see pay figures:** Only People Operations and the employee concerned can see an individual's compensation figures.\n- **No numbers:** The document deliberately leaves out all figures.\n\nIt doesn't say how bands are set, how employees are placed in them, or how recommendations get approved. People Operations should have that detail. I can file a ticket asking them for it if you'd like.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
